   "description": "In the crash-guard reducer, import and bake arms always overwrite inProgress (Android PdfRenderGuardState.arm does the same). An import while a bake runs therefore replaces the bake marker, and complete(.import) clears it. A crash later in that bake gives no bakeInterrupted notice; the work directory is still cleaned at launch. While a bake marker is down, base/vector arms are refused, so live renders of a freshly opened sheet run unguarded for the whole bake. This is contract-level (fixture crashGuard), so both platforms match.",
   "fix": "Contract follow-up: either keep the bake marker in its own slot (a bakeInProgress field) or refuse or queue import arms while a bake marker is down. Add a fixture case for import-during-bake."
  },
  {
   "platform": "both",
   "severity": "minor",
   "file": "docs/THREAT_MODEL.md",
   "description": "The new \u00a79 note says the bake is the only rendered output on disk. But the at-rest bullet 'Data that is still plaintext on disk' still lists only MBTiles packs and imported PDF/GeoPDF sheets. The Generate Offline Tiles MBTiles is a plaintext raster of the AO in offline_tiles and should be listed there. On iOS it is NSFileProtectionCompleteUntilFirstUserAuthentication and isExcludedFromBackup, and the whole offline_tiles directory is now excluded from backup. The guard file is also plaintext, holding only UUIDs.",
   "fix": "Add the baked offline tiles to the plaintext-at-rest bullet, with their location, protection class and backup exclusion, and say that Remove Offline Tiles or Delete Map reaps them via reconcile."
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Verdict: one major issue (iOS bake publish can revert a newer calibration, reproduced), so pass=false. Everything else below is minor or a test gap.\n\nChecked and OK:\n- **Hostile-PDF bounds:**\n  - WP1 caps page coordinates at 1.1e9 and the crop at \u2264 4096 vertices, and toWGS84 range-checks lat/lon.\n  - The footprint rejects area < 1 pt\u00b2 and non-finite values with pageGeometry; mmpp of 0 or non-finite also throws.\n  - The warp planner depth is capped. The staged bitmap is held to \u2264 2\u00d7 job pixels on both platforms; Kotlin toInt saturates.\n  - iOS makeContext limits sides to 16384; the base raster is \u2264 4096 a side.\n  - Passwords give passwordProtected (iOS unlocks with \"\", Android maps SecurityException); missing pages give pageMissing.\n  - Android catches OOM around our own bitmaps and reports it, never as success.\n- **Threading:**\n  - CGPDF objects stay on their own lane, and pdfium is only touched on the single PdfRender thread. The preflight and region renders also go through the executor.\n  - MBTilesStore is locked or @Synchronized on both platforms.\n  - Tile completions hop to main.\n  - The Android bake cancel fix is sound: withContext prompt cancellation would have skipped the old delete.\n- **Durability and storage:**\n  - Guard writes are atomic and fsynced on both platforms (iOS write .atomic + synchronize; Android tmp + fd.sync + ATOMIC_MOVE).\n  - The guard file holds UUID-validated tokens only, in noBackupFilesDir on Android and backup-excluded on iOS.\n  - The iOS bake is fsynced before the rename and the publish happens on main, so it can't interleave with a reconcile.\n  - The Android publish runs under withManagedFilesLock with a compare-and-set attachBake.\n  - No rendered tile reaches disk except the bake. The only other new write is a ~300-byte synthetic PDF for the size probe, in cacheDir and deleted right after.\n  - Android has allowBackup=false and data-extraction rules that exclude everything.\n- **Debug hooks:** compiled out of release on both platforms; see the test fields.\n- **Comments and localization:** no em dashes or backticks in new comments; the localization check passes.\n\nNot covered by any issue (limitations / FYI):\n- **No time budget:** CG and pdfium draws can't be interrupted. A pathological page can hold an iOS lane, or the single Android pdfium thread (blocking all PDF work, including later import probes), indefinitely. The crash guard only covers the first base/vector render per token; later crashes at new zooms aren't caught. Both are contract-level.\n- **Main-thread cost on a hostile neatline:** a 4096-vertex neatline densifies to about 131k vertices, and classify() runs per tile on main (hasContent while planning). Expect jank, not a hang.\n- **PSNR floor:** Android lowered the bake PSNR floor from the design's 35 dB to 30 dB. The implementer flagged this; it needs the benchmark decision.\n- **Stale catalog string:** the \"Bakes this calibrated map\u2026 no desktop tools\" entry is still in the catalog for iOS but no Swift code uses it (contract L says remove it).\n\nScratch artifacts (all under /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-cbrooker-Code-TacticalMaps/d9f42208-9d3f-40e1-9b8b-49fa6c488260/scratchpad/):\n- WP2-render-mut: mutated copy, with review-only tests ios/TacticalMapsTests/ReviewBakeStaleSaveTests.swift and android/app/src/test/java/com/tacmap/map/render/pdf/ReviewBakeEstimateCostTest.kt.\n- Logs: wp2-mut-ios.log, wp2-mut-android.log, wp2-review-estimate.log, wp2-review-ios-full.log.\n- dd-wp2-mut and dd-wp2-release derived data.\n\nThe worktree itself was not modified (git status unchanged). The simulator has the worktree build reinstalled. Emulator-5560 was not touched."
}
